The program's commands with their options, and the environment variables it reads.

\docfield{Version}{\verbcode{0.5.0}}

\section*{Commands}

\begin{docitem}{command}{info}

\docsummary{Describe the environment \{packages, features \& more\}}

\begin{docparams}[Options]
\docparam{PATH}{}{}{A page's path}
\docparam{-r, --recursive}{}{}{Include the pages below in full (100\%)}
\docparam{-p, --profile}{PROFILE}{}{The profile in view (default: \verbcode{html})}
\end{docparams}

\end{docitem}

\section*{Environment variables}

\begin{itemize}
\item \verbcode{FLMPATH}: Folders of extensions, separated by \verbtext{`}:\verbtext{`} (C:\textbackslash{} on Windows \verbtext{~} ;)
\end{itemize}

\section*{More about the program}

\begin{itemize}
\item \docref{program/paths}{The program's folders}: The folders the program reads: the search path of extensions, the folder of the citation cache, the image folders.
\item \docref{program/extensions}{Packages and extensions available}: The packages and extensions a document may use: those compiled into the program, those found on the search path, and those bundled into the program.
\end{itemize}

